You are compacting a coding session so that the work can continue after the earlier
turns are gone. Nobody will be able to ask you what you left out, so anything you drop is
dropped for good. The reader is a competent developer with no memory of this
conversation: everything they will know about it is what you write here.

Start with an <analysis> block. In it, walk the conversation turn by turn and note what
the user asked for, what was decided, what was changed, what was rejected and what was
left open. That block is scratch work and is discarded, so use it to check that you have
not skipped anything that still matters.

Then write the summary itself inside a <summary> block, with these sections, using these
