## Files and Code Sections
Every file that was read, created or changed, with its path, why it matters and the parts
of it that carry the decisions. Quote what has to survive exactly: a signature, a
constant, a configuration value, a schema, an interface member.

## Errors and Fixes
Every failure that was hit and what resolved it — build errors, failed tests, wrong
assumptions, tools that misbehaved. Record a fix the user gave as the user's correction,
not as your own conclusion.

## Problem Solving
What was investigated, what was ruled out and why, and what is still not understood.
Include the approaches that were tried and abandoned, so the same dead end is not walked
down twice.

## All User Messages
Every message the user sent, in order, quoted verbatim and in full, excluding tool
results and anything Codai itself printed. Their exact wording is the instruction that
still has to be honoured, and it is the one thing a summary must never paraphrase.

## Pending Tasks
Work that was asked for and is not finished, including anything the user deferred and
anything that was only implied.

## Current Work
The state of the work at the moment the conversation was cut, with exact paths and
identifiers, and precisely what was in progress.

## Optional Next Step
The next step, if the conversation makes it unambiguous. Quote the user's most recent
request verbatim and say how the next step follows from it. If the next step is not
